From 2cdbce70a7ddf584360a9a4ac8c12d4ce095961d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shizuo Fujita <fujita@clear-code.com>
Date: Thu, 25 Jun 2026 16:03:18 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] buffer, in_http: enforce size limits on decompressed payloads

Enforce a size limit (decompression_size_limit, default 256MB) on
decompressed gzip/deflate payloads in in_http, in_forward and buffer chunks
to prevent decompression bomb denial of service.

[CVE-2026-44160]

[ Upstream commit 2cdbce70a7ddf584360a9a4ac8c12d4ce095961d ]
https://github.com/fluent/fluentd/pull/5393

Signed-off-by: Shizuo Fujita <fujita@clear-code.com>
[Shivani: Backported to fluentd-1.18.0 using the gzip-only variant, as 1.18.0 has no zstd support. Removed test and CHANGELOG changes]
Signed-off-by: Shivani Agarwal <shivani.agarwal@broadcom.com>
---
--- a/lib/fluent/event.rb
+++ b/lib/fluent/event.rb
@@ -268,10 +268,11 @@ module Fluent
   end
 
   class CompressedMessagePackEventStream < MessagePackEventStream
-    def initialize(data, cached_unpacker = nil, size = 0, unpacked_times: nil, unpacked_records: nil)
-      super
+    def initialize(data, cached_unpacker = nil, size = 0, unpacked_times: nil, unpacked_records: nil, decompression_size_limit: Fluent::Plugin::Compressable::DEFAULT_DECOMPRESSION_SIZE_LIMIT)
+      super(data, cached_unpacker, size, unpacked_times: unpacked_times, unpacked_records: unpacked_records)
       @decompressed_data = nil
       @compressed_data = data
+      @decompression_size_limit = decompression_size_limit
     end
 
